# What is the right age for a child to learn drawing?
I don’t think there’s a fixed age, but I’d say around three or four is a good time to start. At that age, children are usually very curious and are beginning to develop their motor skills, so drawing can be a fun way for them to practise using their hands and explore their creativity. However, I think parents should focus more on letting children enjoy drawing rather than teaching them complicated techniques. If they have fun with it from an early age, they may naturally become more interested and improve as they get older.